---
code: unmodeled-wall-inventory
when-fires: a linted book carries at least one unmodeled ⊤-wall; the finding names the FIRST one. lint/source_unmodeled.rs. `{wall_count}`/`{wall_word}` are the census, `{downstream}` the approximate leaf count after the first wall.
why: 27R §2 item-2, the gradual-enhancement nag - silence licenses nothing, so a wall is disclosed with the cost it imposes. The downstream count is APPROXIMATE (all downstream commands, not only the modeled ones) - seam-unmodeled-degradation-count.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
eval "apt-get install -y nginx"
apt-get install -y curl

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
